siveness in epithelial cells</article-title><source>Cancer Res</source><year>2004</year><volume>64</volume><fpage>6579</fpage><lpage>6587</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Cancer Res||64|6579||bib31|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15374971</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib32"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Loewen</surname><given-names>GM</given-names></name><name><surname>Tracy</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Blanchard</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Tan</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Yu</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Raza</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Matsui</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Baumann</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Transformation of human bronchial epithelial cells alters responsiveness to inflammatory cytokines</article-title><source>BMC Cancer</source><year>2005</year><volume>5</volume><fpage>145</fpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'BMC Cancer||5|145||bib32|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16271139</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib33"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Luna</surname><given-names>MC</given-names></name><name><surname>Wong</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Gomer</surname><given-names>CJ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Photodynamic therapy mediated induction of early response genes</article-title><source>Cancer Res</source><year>1994</year><volume>54</volume><fpage>1374</fpage><lpage>1380</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Cancer Res||54|1374||bib33|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8118827</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib34"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Minami</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Inoue</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Wei</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Takeda</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Matsumoto</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Kishimoto</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Akira</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>STAT3 activation is a critical step in gp130-mediated terminal differentiation and growth arrest of a myeloid cell line</article-title><source>Proc Natl Acad Sci USA</source><year>1996</year><volume>93</volume><fpage>3963</fpage><lpage>3966</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Proc Natl Acad Sci USA||93|3963||bib34|'--></citation></ref><ref id="bib35"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Novick</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Shulman</surname><given-names>LM</given-names></name><name><surname>Chen</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Revel</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Enhancement of interleukin 6 cytostatic effect on human breast carcinoma cells by soluble IL-6 receptor from urine and reversion by monoclonal antibody</article-title><source>Cytokine</source><year>1992</year><volume>4</volume><fpage>6</fpage><lpage>11</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Cytokine||4|6||bib35|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1617157</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib36"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Rakemann</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Niehof</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Kubicka</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Fischer</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Manns</surname><given-names>MP</given-names></name><name><surname>Rose-John</surname><given-names>S</given-names>